{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>When you till the ground</b> etc. And the third thing He said to him: <b>A fugitive and a wanderer you shall be in the earth.</b> That he would be driven about and exiled in every place, never resting and never quiet in any one place forever; and He punished him with exile, according to the law of a murderer." "<b>And by way of</b> reason (sekhel): in the names of Cain and Abel there is an arousal and an allusion to the matter of coming-into-being and perishing, for they are brothers adjacent to one another. And Cain alludes to the acquisition of this world, while Abel alludes to one whose mind is humble and who nullifies acquisition. And so his offering was of sheep, which is the lowliest of all living creatures, and therefore the will of HaShem, blessed be He, attached itself to him, as it is written: ״וישע ה׳ אל הבל ואל מנחתו״. And the offering of Cain was of the fruit of the ground, for he loved the acquisitions of this world and bodily labor that has no permanence, and he pursued physical desires; therefore the will of the Holy One, blessed be He, did not rest upon him, as it is written: ״ואל קין ואל מנחתו לא שעה״. This nullifier was killed, for he pays no heed to the affairs of the world and does not make this world the essence; and the lover of this world's acquisitions was cursed, and He said to him: ״נע ונד תהיה בארץ״ — for so one who loves silver is never sated with silver, and he goes and is driven about from place to place, through deserts and wildernesses, in places of beasts and bandits, and he has no rest even for a single hour, but all his days are pains. And Solomon, peace be upon him, alluded to this matter in the book of Ecclesiastes, as he said (Ecclesiastes 2:3): ״תרתי בלבי למשוך ביין את בשרי״. And he said (ibid.): ״הגדלתי מעשי בניתי לי בתים״ etc., ״קניתי עבדים ושפחות״ etc., ״כנסתי לי גם כסף וזהב״. And this encompasses all the acquisitions and attainments of the world, and this corresponds to Cain, for all is vain and all returns to the dust; this is what is said: ״וקין היה עובד אדמה״. And after Solomon, peace be upon him, mentioned the matter of his wealth in all the acquisitions of the world, he mentioned after it: ״ופניתי אני בכל מעשי שעשו ידי ובעמל שעמלתי לעשות והנה הכל הבל ורעות רוח״. Behold, he was aroused concerning the matter of Cain and Abel, in which is alluded coming-into-being and perishing. And afterward he sealed his book with the fear of HaShem, which is the essence of the Torah and the commandments, corresponding to Seth, who was the essence of the sons from whom the world was founded. And it was fitting that this matter be alluded to in the names of human beings born first in the world." "<small>(Belongs above, verse 10.)</small> <b>The voice of your brother's blood.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: his blood and the blood of his seed. And this Midrash alludes to the resurrection of the dead, for since he died, his offspring were no longer in his power — and where is the blood of his seed? Rather, the matter alludes to the resurrection of the dead at the end. Or the blood of his seed may allude to the matter known through the Kabbalah, concerning which Scripture said: ״שת instead of Abel.״ And behold, the punishment of Cain was measure for measure: he intended to cut off his brother's seed, and he and his seed were cut off in the Flood."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:28.404193655Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}